	That install applies to "Virus" © 1988 D.J.Braben.
	Virus Enhanced 2.0b (20.11.2026)
	Original install: John Selck. Version 2.0b: Vesuri.


	That install requires WHDLoad 17 and RawDIC to be in the path.
	Both can be found in the WHDLoad package.
	To install from a different drive than DF0: select Expert as
	installation mode.


	You need 0.6 MB ChipMem and 0.6 MB OtherMem.
	With 620 KB FastMem more, the game runs and draws there.
	You can quit the game by pressing F10 (key can be changed with
	Tooltype "QuitKey=").


	Highscores are saved to HD.

	CUSTOM1=1: Enhanced framerate, set in the installed icon. CUSTOM2 sets
	its game speed: 0 16.7 Hz (the default), 1 25 Hz, 2 12.5 Hz. With
	FastMem it also draws frames interpolated between the game's steps, up
	to 50 a second. 0 or unset runs the game as before.

	version 2.0b (20.11.2026) done by Vesuri:
	- Enhanced framerate (CUSTOM1, on in the installed icon): the game keeps
	  one pace on every Amiga instead of following the frame rate; CUSTOM2
	  picks the game speed
	- the attract screen lasts as long on slower Amigas as on faster ones,
	  and the title at least as long on faster Amigas as on an A1200
	- instruction cache flushed after the game rewrites its renderer
	- the game runs and draws in fast memory when there is enough: faster on
	  68020 and up (the demo: 23 to 47 frames a second on a 50 MHz 68030)
	- Enhanced framerate with FastMem draws frames between the game's steps:
	  up to 50 frames a second

	This game needs 544 KB ChipMem instead of 512 KB because of
	some memory leaks in the render routines which make Virus
	write to some adresses beyond the 512 KB border.


	if you have problems with this installation please try first to get
	a newer version of this install from 
		http://www.fh-zwickau.de/~jah/whdload/
	if that doesn't help try some Tooltypes like NOCACHE, NOAUTOVEC,
	NOVBRMOVE, NOMMU, PAL or NTSC. if that also doesn't help inform the
	author via the Bug-Report-Form which can be accessed on
		http://www.fh-zwickau.de/~jah/whdload/

	for full WHDLoad package and other installs refer to:
		http://www.fh-zwickau.de/~jah/whdload/
	or	aminet:dev/misc/whdload#?
	and	aminet:game/patch/


